From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 09:07:17 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: import host memory into a linear modifier image

Imported host memory becomes a MTLBuffer and never a MTLHeap, so an image over
it has to be a texture over a buffer: a linear layout. The image format query
enforced that by naming VK_IMAGE_TILING_LINEAR exactly, which leaves out the
other linear layout this driver has, DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR. That modifier is
the same MTLBuffer-backed layout under a name an importer can agree on, and it
is the only modifier offered, so the query already checked it before reaching
here and kk_image_layout_calc_linear() lays it out the same way.

Excluding it had a cost. A paired Venus renderer reaches this driver through
VK_EXT_external_memory_host for every guest dma-buf, and uses the modifier
form for a shareable image because plain linear tiling is not a colour
attachment here. Those two rules together left a guest with no image that is
both shareable and renderable: gbm_bo_create() succeeded only as an optimal
image that cannot be exported, gbm_bo_get_fd() failed, and an
EGL_EXT_image_dma_buf_import of a linear modifier image was refused outright.

Ask the question the layout actually answers: whether the image is laid out
linearly at all, which kk_tiling_is_linear_layout() already decides for both
tilings and the driver's meson test pins.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image.c
index 31a7d463df8df2bab38bc776b038815361ea3fda..af698e9d6772579bf46f056b89fea6dd390ac296 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image.c
@@ -501,7 +501,13 @@ kk_GetPhysicalDeviceImageFormatProperties2(
          break;
       case VK_EXTERNAL_MEMORY_HANDLE_TYPE_HOST_ALLOCATION_BIT_EXT:
       case VK_EXTERNAL_MEMORY_HANDLE_TYPE_HOST_MAPPED_FOREIGN_MEMORY_BIT_EXT: {
-         if (pImageFormatInfo->tiling != VK_IMAGE_TILING_LINEAR) {
+         /* Imported host memory becomes a MTLBuffer and never a MTLHeap, so
+          * such an image has to be a texture over a buffer, which is what a
+          * linear layout is. DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR is that same layout under
+          * a name an importer can agree on, and it is the only modifier this
+          * driver offers, so it qualifies as well: the modifier was already
+          * checked above, and a modifier image is laid out linearly. */
+         if (!linear_layout) {
             return vk_errorf(pdev, VK_ERROR_FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED,
                              "host memory import image must be linear");
          }
